        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/FRdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGesQAHpauSGWwWU7ckEWOba5MzGe\npMo63AADZuobpNqxCSbPQ0Dbv/TEbcjRMsXzV6qeGe3KlQga5ORMb+F6NqvkO5Te\niY5JYdicHT9r/lo8UpWZEJHy68udZrEgXpOLwFM4ljTkaz6LTuNn9P7oKidOqPlc\nP4yFPAq4LGCS1T3kPQRUJYqC7FZW9gqwNnyMaDSTMJkD+PooAVXJg8r4SDDTsNB4\n8z0896fTuFJuFQ1RKDghigLiB3OKYdGaTTKmhaS6CSOtUEV4sOzUyYDIj2ZPWDvW\nWfzyha1PyGGtvfX03ihCDy0jDy1E64OEuCD0CBxyTsDvfwKdNaztIPYPcrxi3MwW\n8dn2PbVE1kgc56qfSrSpbU8AGQcyc3fMtefWu+jXGEtf95A6hlUX2bq+kaxSBMDr\nfOx6dM7nRNRBNfkOnoyf7YQ5i3nWKGDwd3DtLpabtptzE+xMUBFY9X96fG0V+CkV\nZckQe8nuRNdXejTG+f3T2CRGWgLYPrDrlYdFYS73hjOg0148a1BHyN+UwJz7jjj6\nZ1L9E/+qBZThzGvjh3crLxqWL7dWGE4ZICMi213jRvjTOIt8js7sZ5NpoNA7RjPk\npPRFAOEOc0ZwhfJfeNQzlj3ovLshFlj6cc27xE/HdVtA5fuirj1B1BMW1xU4jnQc\n7UZ3OX2ETRq6KhhKFF+r\n=vpdG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree 61b602ce0ddb516f686fcf0fd1ccfbe7047d76d9\nparent a35a02f8dfff5bb3f268613e82ae19747f154b17\nauthor rabble <evan@protest.net> 1778144349 +1200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778144349 +1200\n\nfix(video): show event description on video page, not title-as-content (#343)\n\nThe Funnelcake transform was mapping `raw.title` into `ParsedVideoData.content`\n(\"Funnelcake uses title field for content\"). VideoCard guards against\nduplicating the title by rendering content only when it differs from the\ntitle, so the actual Nostr `content` field — the user-authored description —\nnever made it to the page.\n\nMap `raw.content` through instead. The single-video endpoint\n(`/api/videos/{id}`) already populates `raw.content` from `event.content`\nin `fetchVideoById`. List endpoints that omit content fall through to an\nempty string, which the existing VideoCard guard already handles.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
